# Line endings are normalised so a checkout on Windows and a checkout on Linux
# hold byte-identical files. Without this, core.autocrlf=true rewrites every
# PHP file to CRLF in the working copy while the committed blob stays LF, and
# PHPCS then reports "End of line character is invalid" against a file that is
# perfectly fine in the repository.
#
# `eol=lf` (not just `text=auto`) is what actually pins the working copy: with
# `text=auto` alone the checkout still follows core.autocrlf, so the phantom
# error survives. Nothing here rewrites committed content — the blobs are
# already LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by end-of-line conversion. The screenshot
# baselines in tests/baselines/ are irreplaceable, and a single byte of CRLF
# mangling would destroy them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
